          "Before adding a new timekeeping item, check whether the request already exists under another name or channel. For each open timekeeping, record the source, the client intake, the decision, and the destination field before moving to the next item. Close the day by checking that each completed timekeeping has a destination update in the team roster and a confirmation for the requester. When a case moves between owners, require an acknowledgment before the old owner stops watching it. At Outsourced Company, the October 28 timekeeping review should name the backup owner and the coverage window.",
          "Open the timekeeping queue in the timekeeping system and mark every item with the current owner, the next action, and the time it is due. When the next step belongs to client sponsor, write the request and the due time instead of leaving the case in a waiting state. The end-of-day review should show what was completed, what is blocked, who owns the next step, and which team roster is still missing. A daily stand-up should review exceptions and aging items, not read every completed ticket aloud. The October 28 timekeeping exception log should show the reason code, owner, and release decision."
