          "Track repeated exceptions separately from one-off errors; a pattern may point to a form, a queue rule, or a permissions problem. An escalation packet should include the timekeeping link, verified facts, the unresolved decision, the deadline, actions already taken, and the safest next step. A stop is not a failure of service; it is the control working before the error reaches operations manager. A workaround used during an outage in the timekeeping system should have an expiry time and a reconciliation owner. The October 28 timekeeping recovery test should record the restore point and the quality review pass rate result.",
