          "Start the evidence map by naming the field in the task queue that the access change action is supposed to change. Keep the original client intake and the corrected version side by side, with the reason for the change and the person who approved it. After the conflict is resolved, add a short correction entry to the access change log and link it to both source versions. Keep the client intake in the approved repository and link it to the access change case instead of attaching it to a personal message. At Outsourced Company, record the October 28 access change correction and link it to the original source.",
          "For access change, the governing source is the team roster; a note in the queue is only a pointer to that source. If the team roster contains sensitive data, store it in the approved location and record only the minimum reference needed for the access change review. Use a separate reason code for conflicting evidence so the pattern can be reviewed without reading every message. If the team roster contains personal or confidential data, use the approved access path and record only the reference in the queue. The operations manager decision on access change should be dated October 28 and linked to the team roster."
