          "When unowned task is involved, use the highest escalation path even if the access change request looks routine. When the decision is urgent, call out the consequence of waiting and the last safe time to act. Record the stop time, the reason, and the release decision so the delay can be reviewed without guessing. Reason codes should be short enough to use at the queue and specific enough to route the case to the right owner. The October 28 access change recovery test should record the restore point and the quality review pass rate result.",
          "Use separate reason codes for missing quality review, conflicting source, wrong access change, expired approval, unavailable team lead, and an outage in the access management console. After the decision, link the response to the destination change and close the exception with the reason it occurred. If access is wrong or unexplained, stop the access change work before opening the access management console with borrowed credentials. If the same exception appears in three cases, review the intake form or the quality review requirement. For the October 28 review at Outsourced Company, log the access change check with the quality review and the timekeeping exception rate result.",
