          "In outsourced operations, client intake often begins as a small favor from operations manager, which makes it easy to skip the evidence that would let someone else reconstruct the decision. Without a visible owner, the request can sit in a shared inbox while everyone assumes someone else has checked the timekeeping system. The operating standard should distinguish preparation from approval and show both in the same client intake trail. The control should also cover the quiet case: an item that sits open because nobody knows who owns the next step. The operations manager decision on client intake should be dated October 28 and linked to the client report."
