          "The client intake evidence set should include the request, the client intake, the owner decision, the action taken, and the final value in the access management console. Attach the client intake to the case, label its version or date, and record the field in the access management console that it supports. Resolve the conflict by naming the authoritative source, the owner who decided, and the correction applied to the access management console. A late client intake is still evidence, but it should not be presented as if it existed at the time of the first decision. The October 28 client intake close should name the destination field, the approver, and the rework rate check.",
          "Do not treat a forwarded email as the record itself when the governing value lives in the reporting dashboard; the email may explain intent, but it does not replace the field. The reviewer should be able to open the team roster from the case without searching a personal drive or asking for a screenshot. A conflict is not a reason to rewrite history; it is a reason to show the reviewer exactly where the client intake record stopped agreeing with itself. A source that cannot be opened by the reviewer is not a usable source, even if the operator can see it on their screen. At Outsourced Company, the October 28 client intake review should name the backup owner and the coverage window."
