          "Start with the cases that affect excess access, then move to routine requests; age alone is not the only priority signal. If the operator touches the task queue, record the before-and-after value and the approval that allowed the change. Record any correction made during the day and link it to the original task queue record. If the queue is too large to review, split it by risk or channel rather than sampling only the newest items. The October 28 control note for Outsourced Company should name the task queue source, the owner, and the next review time.",
