          "A missing team roster and an unreadable team roster are different exceptions and should not share the same reason code. An escalation that ends in silence should remain open; silence is not approval. If the exception affects stale client report, pause the dependent action until offshore worker decides and the decision is recorded. When a case is blocked by access, record the system, the role requested, and the person who can grant it. The task queue review at Outsourced Company should state whether the team roster was current on October 28.",
          "A missing task record and an unreadable task record are different exceptions and should not share the same reason code. Keep the escalation in the task queue case so the response is visible to the next reviewer. When the source is unavailable, do not substitute a familiar value from an earlier task queue; stop and record the gap. A workaround used during an outage in the access management console should have an expiry time and a reconciliation owner. On October 28, Outsourced Company should compare the task queue queue count with the timekeeping exception rate denominator."
